From d1e4ed566f5c4ca7f53340e009f20b508ce8b098 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:41:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/79] nouveau/vk: build a static driver where there is no
 dynamic loader
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An ICD is two things: a shared object the Vulkan loader dlopen()s, and a
JSON manifest telling the loader which file to open. Neither means
anything on a platform that has no dynamic loader. There is no loader
process to read the manifest, and nothing that could open the library if
there were, so the shared library is dead weight and the manifest names
a file nobody will ever look for.

Building it also fails outright when the static libraries it links are
not position-independent, which is the normal state of a build for a
platform with no shared libraries at all:

  ERROR: Can't link non-PIC static library 'nvk' into shared library
         'vulkan_nouveau'. Use the 'pic' option to static_library to
         build with PIC.

Where there is no dlopen, libnvk is therefore declared as a dependency
and the shared library and both manifests are skipped. An application on
such a platform links the driver directly and enters it through
vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr, which is in the archive.

with_dlopen is the same condition meson.build already uses to decide
whether anything can be loaded at run time.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 — the nouveau Vulkan driver for Horizon
Why: Horizon has no dynamic loader (patch 0001 records that dlopen,
  libdl and dlfcn.h are all absent on newlib/libnx), so an ICD .so and
  its manifest cannot be used. The driver has to be linked into the
  application.
Evidence: configuring mesa-26.1.5 for aarch64/horizon with
  -Dvulkan-drivers=nouveau stops at
    src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build:160:20: ERROR: Can't link non-PIC
    static library 'nvk' into shared library 'vulkan_nouveau'.
  With this change the same command configures.
Upstream: yes — it is conditional on a property Mesa already computes,
  and changes nothing on any platform that has a loader.
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build b/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
index 21b66e8..37d8709 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -157,6 +157,23 @@ libnvk = static_library(
   gnu_symbol_visibility : 'hidden',
 )
 
+# An ICD is a shared object the Vulkan loader dlopen()s, and a manifest
+# telling it which file to open. Neither means anything on a platform
+# with no dynamic loader: there is no loader process to read the JSON,
+# and nothing that could open the library if there were. On such a
+# platform the driver is linked into the application, which reaches it
+# through vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr in the static archive.
+#
+# with_dlopen is the same condition meson.build already uses to decide
+# whether anything can be loaded at run time at all.
+if not with_dlopen
+  idep_nvk = declare_dependency(
+    link_whole : libnvk,
+    dependencies : nvk_deps,
+  )
+  subdir_done()
+endif
+
 libvulkan_nouveau = shared_library(
   'vulkan_nouveau',
   link_whole : [libnvk],
-- 
2.43.0

